      "dcterms:title": "Representation of the Quantum Plane, its Quantum Double and Harmonic Analysis on GL+_q(2,R)",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "Double",
        "GL+, Harmonic Analysis on"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20180603",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1108.5365",
      "dcterms:abstract": "We give complete detail of the description of the GNS representation of the quantum plane A and its dual ˆ A as a von Neumann algebra. In particu- lar we obtain a rather surprising result that the multiplicative unitary W is manageable in this quantum semigroup context. We study the quantum dou- ble group construction introduced by Woronowicz, and using Baaj and Vaes’ construction of the multiplicative unitary Wm, we give the GNS description of the quantum double D(A) which is equivalent to GL+ q (2, R). Furthermore we study the fundamental corepresentation T λ,t and its matrix coeﬃcients, and show that it can be expressed by the b-hypergeometric function. We also study the regular corepresentation and representation induced by Wm, and prove that the space of L2 functions on the quantum double decomposes into the continuous series representation of Uqeq(gl(2, R)) with the quantum dilogarithm |Sb(Q + 2iα)|2 as the Plancherel measure. Finally we describe certain representation theoretic meaning of integral transforms involving the quantum dilogarithm function. ∗Kavli IPMU, The University of Tokyo, 5-1-5 Kashiwanoha, Kashiwa, 277-8583, Chiba, Japan Email: ivan.ip@ipmu.jp 1",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-1108.5365v2/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-1108.5365v2"
    }
  ]
